- Young Serif (https://github.com/nootype/young-serif) —
  SIL Open Font License 1.1
  Copyright (c) 2017 The Young Serif Project Authors.

- Datatype — bundled for experimentation. Licensing per upstream;
  contributors should verify before redistribution.

A ShieldFont built from these OFL base fonts is a derivative work — a
Modified Version in OFL terms. Rendering is modified via injected OpenType
GSUB ligature rules; glyph outlines from each base font remain intact.

If you build one, YOU MUST NOT put the base typeface's Reserved Font Name
in the name of your font, including its internal name table. OFL §3 forbids
it and §5 terminates the licence for a breach, so a build named e.g.
"ShieldFont Inter" would lose the very grant that permitted it. Name your
build after your own project or foundry and credit the base typeface in the
Description field (nameID 10), which carries no such restriction. See
docs/custom-faces.md.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Optik — the typeface behind the shipped default variants
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The default variants this project ships (the shieldfont-alpha / -beta /
-gamma / -maxhide downloads and the CDN/React optik-* builds) are built on
Optik, a proprietary typeface © Playtype <https://playtype.com>. Optik is
NOT open-source and NOT under the SIL Open Font License.

  Playtype permits ShieldFont to ship and use Optik, whether or not the
  word substitutions are active, provided the use is within the ShieldFont
  packages and tooling. The glyph outlines are the original Optik; only the
  decoy glyph names and the font's own metadata (family/version) are altered.
  This permission covers the Optik-derived variants distributed with
  ShieldFont, including rendering them with the substitutions turned off
  (see the <NonShield> component in @shieldfont/react). Optik itself remains
  © Playtype and is not offered under an open-source license — do not
  extract or redistribute the Optik outlines outside ShieldFont, and do not
  use them as a general-purpose typeface outside it.

The SIL Open Font License (LICENSE-FONTS) applies only to variants you build
yourself from an OFL base font (e.g. Inter) via scripts/generate_font.py.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lexical databases used to build language mappings
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Lexique 3.83 (http://www.lexique.org) — Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0.
  New, B., Pallier, C., Ferrand, L., & Matos, R. (2001). Une base de
  données lexicales du français contemporain sur internet: LEXIQUE.
  L'Année Psychologique, 101, 447-462.

  Used by scripts/build_fr_pairs.py for French part-of-speech, gender,
  number and verb inflection. The database is downloaded on demand and
  cached in scripts/lexicon/ (gitignored); it is NOT redistributed by this
  project. What this repository commits is the derived mapping — a set of
  seeded random word pairs — and the pipeline that produces it.

  Whether that derived mapping is Adapted Material under CC BY-SA 4.0 is a
  question a maintainer should answer deliberately rather than by default,
  since the answer decides whether the French mapping can ship under this
  repository's licence alone. It is raised here rather than assumed away.

